    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 all tests green. Let me summarize what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added optional, validated-when-present `postcode` support to owners. The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, AcceptanceTest 3/3).\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **API contract** \u2014 `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`: added a `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema (`type: string`, `pattern: ^[0-9]{4}$`, not required). It's inherited by `OwnerDto`, so the generated DTOs carry it and it's returned in responses. MapStruct maps it by name.\n\n2. **Domain + persistence** \u2014 added a `postcode` column to `Owner` (`model/Owner.java`) and to all four schema.sql files (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres, `VARCHAR(4)`). Fixed the hsqldb positional seed inserts in `data.sql` (added the extra `NULL`) so the seed load stays valid.\n\n3. **Validation step** \u2014 new `ValidateOwnerPostcode` function: skips when the postcode is null/blank (backward-compatible); otherwise requires exactly 4 digits and, when the city maps to a known region, enforces the range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Unknown-region cities accept any 4-digit code. It reuses the existing `LocalityLookup.regionFor` for the city\u2192region table.\n\n4. **Error handling** \u2014 new checked `InvalidOwnerPostcodeException` + `InvalidOwnerPostcodeExceptionHandler` (responds 400 with `{\"errors\":[\"postcode\"]}`, matching the existing owner-validation error shape) + the escalation YAML wiring.\n\n5. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 inserted the `postcode` step into `owners.POST.yml` (after address normalization) and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml`; `ApplyOwner` now also copies `postcode` on update. `BuildOwner` gets it for free via the mapper.\n\nThe three acceptance tests confirm: a valid postcode is stored and returned, an owner without a postcode is still accepted, and a malformed postcode (`\"12\"`) is rejected with 400.",
